From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 9999999: a generated interface name must be free in the registry it is written into

wifi_gen_first_ifname() offers wlan2, wlan2-1, ... and asks
check_wireless_ifname() whether a candidate is taken. That function looks in one
place only: wifi-iface sections in /etc/config/wireless.

Since 989 that is the wrong place. A BSS that is a link of an AP-MLD gets no
wireless section - uci_apply_wps_credentials() writes the mapagent 'ap' section
and skips the wireless one, on purpose, because the network is already on the
air as a link of the MLD and an extra BSS would take a slot the MLD needs. On a
node whose fronthaul and backhaul are both AP-MLDs, /etc/config/wireless
therefore holds ap_mld_1, ap_mld_2 and sta_mld_1 and not a single wifi-iface.
check_wireless_ifname() consequently answers "free" for every candidate, its
max_bss cap never fires either (it counts the same empty set), and every caller
is handed index 0 - the same name.

Measured on the controller 2026-09-04:

  .1 controller  @ap[4].ifname='wlan2'  @ap[5].ifname='wlan2'   collision
                 no wlan1-1, no wlan2-1
  .2 (healthy)   wlan0, wlan0-1, wlan1, wlan1-1, wlan2-1, wlan2
  .4             same wlan2 collision

Both colliding sections on .1 are anonymous and carry map-agent's own option
order (ifname, band, device, ssid, key, ...) rather than map_genconfig's
(device, ifname, mode, disabled, ...), the same fingerprint 989 used - so both
were generated here, not inherited.

The collision is not caught downstream. config.c logs

  Duplicate 'ap wlan2' config!! ignore

and then keeps going, filling the *same* netif_apcfg with the second section's
options: one section silently leaves the model. And "multiap clean_stale_ifaces
wlan2" deletes by ifname, so when either one is torn down both are removed at
once. Since re->aplist is built exclusively from 'ap' sections (agent.c:4762),
the section that vanishes takes its AP-MLD link with it - not in the TTLM map
(agent_tlv.c:4809-4826), assoc_control returning -1 on `if (!ap || !ap->cfg)`
(agent.c:6198-6200), invisible to steering and to num_sta.

Ask the registry the name is actually written into. cfg->aplist is the in-memory
image of the mapagent 'ap' sections, and uci_apply_wps_credentials() adds a new
entry to it through create_fronthaul_iface_config() before it writes UCI, so a
name handed out earlier in the same M2 loop is already visible - which is
exactly the case that produced the duplicate. The wireless scan stays: on a
platform that does have per-BSS wifi-iface sections it is still a real answer,
and the two tests are a union, never a substitute for each other.

The name test ignores 'device' because these are netdev names and a collision
across radios is as fatal as one on the same radio - the same rule the wireless
loop below already follows, which breaks on an ifname match without looking at
the device. Only the max_bss count is per radio. That count now includes the
bhmld_ap_<band> bookkeeping placeholders, which occupy no BSS slot; that is
conservative rather than wrong, it fails towards refusing to generate rather
than towards handing out a duplicate, and on MT7996 max_bss is 16 against a
count that reaches 3. A max_bss of 0 - which agent_alloc_radio() never
produces, but a driver's radio status could - skips the cap rather than
blocking generation outright.

Left alone deliberately: the "Duplicate 'ap %s' config!! ignore" path in
config.c, which warns and then merges anyway. It is a poor last line of defence,
but it is a last line of defence for a state that should not be reachable, and
changing it to discard a section would delete configuration on the strength of a
name clash. Fix the generator; revisit that only if a duplicate is ever seen
again.

How to tell this worked, on hardware: after a sysupgrade,

  uci show mapagent | grep "\.ifname=" | grep wlan | sort

on the controller must list six distinct names - wlan0, wlan0-1, wlan1, wlan1-1,
wlan2, wlan2-1 - with no value appearing twice, matching what agent .2 already
had, and "logread | grep Duplicate" must be empty for the boot.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/agent_map.c
+++ b/src/agent_map.c
@@ -1828,12 +1828,62 @@
 	struct uci_package *pkg;
 	struct uci_element *e;
 	struct wifi_radio_element *re = agent_get_radio_by_name(a, device);
+	struct netif_apcfg *apcfg = NULL;
 	bool rv = false;
 	int num_ifs = 0;
+	int num_aps = 0;
 
 	if (!re)
 		return -1;
 
+	/* Ask the registry the generated name is actually written into.
+	 *
+	 * The uci_foreach below looks for wifi-iface sections in
+	 * /etc/config/wireless, but since 989 map-agent deliberately does not
+	 * create a wireless section for a BSS that is a link of an AP-MLD - it
+	 * writes the mapagent 'ap' section only. On an all-MLD node wireless
+	 * therefore holds ap_mld_1/ap_mld_2/sta_mld_1 and not one wifi-iface,
+	 * so this function answered "free" for every candidate, and
+	 * wifi_gen_first_ifname() handed out index 0 - the same name - to every
+	 * caller.
+	 *
+	 * Measured on the controller 2026-09-04: radio2 carried two anonymous
+	 * 'ap' sections, both ifname='wlan2', both with map-agent's own option
+	 * order (ifname, band, device, ssid, ...), i.e. both generated here.
+	 * config.c then logs "Duplicate 'ap wlan2' config!! ignore" and fills
+	 * the *same* netif_apcfg from the second section, so the backhaul BSS
+	 * silently left the model, and 'clean_stale_ifaces wlan2' would delete
+	 * both sections at once because it deletes by ifname. A healthy node
+	 * has wlan0, wlan0-1, wlan1, wlan1-1, wlan2, wlan2-1.
+	 *
+	 * cfg->aplist is the in-memory image of those 'ap' sections and
+	 * uci_apply_wps_credentials() adds to it before it writes UCI, so a
+	 * name handed out earlier in the same M2 loop is already visible here.
+	 *
+	 * Names are netdev names: a collision across radios is just as fatal as
+	 * one on the same radio, so the name test ignores 'device' - the same
+	 * rule the wireless loop below already follows. Only the max_bss count
+	 * is per radio, and counting a bookkeeping placeholder there fails safe
+	 * (max_bss is 16 on MT7996, the count reaches 3).
+	 *
+	 * The cap is skipped when max_bss is zero. agent_alloc_radio() seeds it
+	 * with WIFI_IFACE_MAX_NUM, but a driver reporting 0 in its radio status
+	 * would overwrite that, and "generate nothing at all" is not what a zero
+	 * should mean here - it did not mean it before this patch either,
+	 * because the wireless loop below only reaches its own copy of this test
+	 * after it has found a wifi-iface section.
+	 */
+	list_for_each_entry(apcfg, &a->cfg.aplist, list) {
+		if (!strncmp(apcfg->name, ifname, IFNAMSIZ))
+			return true;
+
+		if (!strncmp(apcfg->device, device, IFNAMSIZ))
+			num_aps++;
+	}
+
+	if (re->max_bss && num_aps >= re->max_bss)
+		return true;
+
 	ctx = uci_alloc_context();
 	if (!ctx)
 		return -1;
